<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span><span id="A4.T5.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Per-latent silhouette</span> <math id="A4.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> .
Dashes indicate unused latents in the GSM8K run (here <math id="A4.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{L}{=}12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{L}{=}12</annotation></semantics></math>).
Large-scale pretraining shows uniformly negative silhouettes (cluster intermixing);
GSM8K with curriculum hovers near zero (weak separation);
Countdown exhibits strong separation for most latents while still showing redundancy in cross-subspace capture (see main-text heatmaps).</figcaption>
</figure>
